  "notes": "Ideal rocksalt structural model following Roth (1958), Introduction and Fig. 1; conventional Fm-3m cell with four Ni and four O. The reference edge is normalized to Campbell Table 1 V0, not claimed as a separate ambient cubic refinement. Roth establishes cubic paramagnetic NiO and a rhombohedral distortion below the Neel temperature (523 K at ambient pressure). Campbell reports B1 and fits one cubic-average volume model, including low-temperature MAP points; this record cannot predict magnetic ordering, rhombohedral splitting, or the pressure-dependent Neel boundary. Use the separate nickel_oxide rhombohedral card for resolved low-temperature diffraction.",
